{"resultsCount":5,"resultsLimit":10,"resultsOffset":0,"headlines":[{"id":50036932,"nowId":"1-50036932","contentKey":"50036932-1-5-1","dataSourceIdentifier":"e2baae02d6299","publishedkey":"50036932","type":"HeadlineNews","feedDisplayType":"Default","headline":"Alcaraz outlasts Fritz as Europe takes 7-5 lead in Laver Cup","description":"Carlos Alcaraz saved two match points before finishing off Taylor Fritz 6-3, 4-6, 13-11 on Saturday as Team Europe took a 7-5 lead in the Laver Cup.","title":"Alcaraz outlasts Fritz as Europe takes 7-5 lead in Laver Cup","linkText":"Alcaraz gets revenge, outlasts Fritz as Europe takes 7-5 lead in Laver Cup","categorized":"2026-09-27T12:31:07Z","originallyPosted":"2026-09-26T22:37:19Z","lastModified":"2026-09-26T22:47:12Z","published":"2026-09-26T22:47:12Z","root":"tennis","section":"Tennis","source":"Associated Press","images":[{"dataSourceIdentifier":"b44ccd774774d","id":50037014,"type":"header","name":"Carlos Alcaraz [600x400]","credit":"Photo by Julian Finney/Getty Images for Laver Cup","height":400,"width":600,"url":"https://a.espncdn.com/photo/2026/0926/r1722213_600x400_3-2.jpg"}],"related":[{"id":50029830,"dataSourceIdentifier":"97a2908fe9d74","publishedkey":"50029830","type":"HeadlineNews","headline":"Alcaraz-Mensik doubles win gives Europe 3-1 lead in Laver Cup","title":"Alcaraz-Mensik doubles win gives Europe 3-1 lead in Laver Cup","linkText":"Alcaraz helps Europe to 3-1 Laver Cup lead after opening day","source":"Associated Press","images":[{"dataSourceIdentifier":"5eaaeeac7ab05","id":50029878,"type":"header","name":"Alcaraz - Mensik Laver Cup [1296x729]","credit":"Photo by ANDY RAIN/EPA/Shutterstock","height":729,"width":1296,"url":"https://a.espncdn.com/photo/2026/0925/r1721857_1296x729_16-9.jpg"}],"isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50029830"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50029830"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/general/tennis/story?storyId=50029830"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/story/_/id/50029830/alcaraz-mensik-doubles-win-gives-team-europe-3-1-laver-cup-lead-team-world"}},"premium":false}],"categories":[{"id":9581,"type":"league","uid":"s:850","guid":"aa07e63d-cf6e-3705-9c8d-8d5208e6af14","description":"Tennis","sportId":850,"leagueId":850,"league":{"id":850,"description":"Tennis","links":{"mobile":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/"}},"web":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/"}}}}},{"id":154815,"type":"league","uid":"s:850~l:851","guid":"5e8354a9-d251-395d-a129-c769bd698637","description":"ATP","sportId":851,"leagueId":851,"league":{"id":851,"description":"ATP","abbreviation":"ATP","links":{"mobile":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/"}},"web":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/"}}}}},{"id":463146,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:850~l:851~a:3782","guid":"07843754-8bdf-63b0-5983-24252738169e","description":"Carlos Alcaraz","sportId":851,"athleteId":3782,"athlete":{"id":3782,"description":"Carlos Alcaraz","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/player/_/id/3782/carlos-alcaraz"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/player/_/id/3782/carlos-alcaraz"}}}}},{"id":160065,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:850~l:851~a:2946","guid":"6493155f-cacc-7aa5-ba78-d952efa4c652","description":"Taylor Fritz","sportId":851,"athleteId":2946,"athlete":{"id":2946,"description":"Taylor Fritz","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/player/_/id/2946/taylor-fritz"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/player/_/id/2946/taylor-fritz"}}}}},{"id":409224,"type":"topic","guid":"52313677-19f8-b106-ec91-d8d17e6087fe","description":"news","sportId":0,"topicId":781}],"keywords":["Tennis","ATP","Carlos Alcaraz","Taylor Fritz","news"],"story":"<p>LONDON -- <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=3782\">Carlos Alcaraz</a> squirmed his way out of trouble, saving two match points before producing a drop shot that ended a 6-3, 4-6, 13-11 revenge win over <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2946\">Taylor Fritz</a> as Team Europe took a 7-5 lead in the Laver Cup on Saturday.</p>\n<p>Fritz's only career victory over Alcaraz came during Team World's win over Europe in last year's Laver Cup and the American had his chances to beat the Spaniard again.</p>\n<p>But Alcaraz served an ace on Fritz's first match point and then used a drop shot to save another, and Alcaraz finally won it on his third match point when Fritz got to his drop shot but couldn't get it back.</p>\n<p>\"The drop shot is part of my game,\" Alcaraz said. \"So in those moments, in those really close and important moments, I tried to use it because it was a really good weapon for me in this match and obviously I've been practicing the drops since I was a little kid.\"</p>\n<p><alsosee></p>\n<p>Fritz played a clean match with only nine unforced errors to Alcaraz's 30. But Alcaraz led 42-20 in winners - often bringing the O2 Arena crowd to its feet, as <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=425\">Roger Federer</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=235\">Andy Murray</a> applauded from the front row.</p>\n<p>It was Alcaraz's first singles match since he lost to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=9250\">Ben Shelton</a> in a US Open quarterfinal that ended at 3:33 a.m. He won a doubles match with <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=10319\">Jakub Mensik</a> on Friday.</p>\n<p>Earlier, it was all Team World -- which is captained by <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/andre-agassi-laver-cup-john-mcenroe-07244b768cf7a6393e3e99032051a982\">Andre Agassi</a> -- as <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2651\">Alex de Minaur</a> had a 2-6, 7-6 (5), 11-9 comeback victory over <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2375\">Alexander Zverev</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=10386\">Learner Tien</a> outlasted <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=7602\">Flavio Cobolli</a> 6-3, 2-6, 10-7.</p>\n<p>In the final match of the day, Zverev partnered with <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2989\">Casper Ruud</a> to beat <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2865\">Alexander Bublik</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=3774\">Brandon Nakashima</a> 6-4, 7-6 (7) in doubles.</p>\n<p>Wins are worth one point on Friday, two points on Saturday and three points on Sunday. The first team to reach 13 points wins.</p>\n<p>De Minaur had blood trickling down his right leg after a diving volley he produced in the match tiebreaker against Zverev.</p>\n<p>\"If you can notice, my blood is red as well,\" De Minaur said, referring to the color of Team World's shirts. \"It was a very tough match. A tough battle. I left it all out there and got fortunate in the end to get the job done and happy to give some points for Team World.\"</p>\n<p>Europe had led 3-1 after Friday's play.</p>\n<p>\"We were in the same position last year and it worked out pretty well for us,\" de Minaur said. \"We know we can do some damage. We know we're the underdogs, but we also know that we can step out on this court and light it up.\"</p>\n<p>Zverev served for the match in the second set but double-faulted to hand de Minaur a break and the Australian stormed back into it.</p>\n<p>Early in the match tiebreaker, de Minaur leaped for a volley and ended up sprawled on the black court before popping back up as Zverev's reply sailed out.</p>\n<p>A few points later, Zverev also went down in a worrisome moment but appeared uninjured after his feet slipped out from under him as he hit a backhand.</p>\n<p>Zverev then wasted a match point when he played passively and chipped a forehand wide.</p>\n<p>There was more caution from Zverev on de Minaur's first match point as the French Open and US Open champion hit a weak overhead to let the Australian back into the point. De Minaur then produced a backhand up the line that Zverev couldn't get back.</p>\n<p>How did de Minaur keep believing?</p>\n<p>\"Keep asking questions. Give yourself a chance. And you never know if you put the ball in the court, you might get lucky,\" he said. \"So that's what I did today.\"</p>\n<p>Zverev's defeat ended his nine-match winning streak after the second-ranked player had followed his US Open title with two Davis Cup victories for Germany last weekend.</p>\n<p>The day's opening match also had drama.</p>\n<p>On Tien's first match point, he produced a blistering forehand passing shot that Cobolli could barely get his racket on to conclude a 34-shot rally.</p>\n<p>The 13th-ranked Tien was making his Laver Cup debut.</p>\n<p>Europe has won the Laver Cup five times while Team World took its third title in last year's edition of the Ryder Cup-style event.</p>\n<p>Yannick Noah is Europe's captain.</p>\n\n","allowAMP":true,"allowAds":true,"allowComments":true,"allowCommerce":true,"allowContentReactions":true,"allowSearch":true,"isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50036932"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50036932"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/general/tennis/story?storyId=50036932"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/story/_/id/50036932/alcaraz-outlasts-fritz-europe-takes-7-5-lead-laver-cup"}},"premium":false},{"id":50029830,"nowId":"1-50029830","contentKey":"50029830-1-5-1","dataSourceIdentifier":"97a2908fe9d74","publishedkey":"50029830","type":"HeadlineNews","feedDisplayType":"Default","headline":"Alcaraz-Mensik doubles win gives Europe 3-1 lead in Laver Cup","description":"Team Europe took a 3-1 lead over Team World on Friday's opening day of the Laver Cup after Carlos Alcaraz and Jakub Mensik sealed the final point with a doubles victory in London.","title":"Alcaraz-Mensik doubles win gives Europe 3-1 lead in Laver Cup","linkText":"Alcaraz helps Europe to 3-1 Laver Cup lead after opening day","categorized":"2026-09-27T12:31:07Z","originallyPosted":"2026-09-25T23:28:41Z","lastModified":"2026-09-27T12:31:06Z","published":"2026-09-27T12:31:06Z","root":"tennis","section":"Tennis","source":"Associated Press","images":[{"dataSourceIdentifier":"5eaaeeac7ab05","id":50029878,"type":"header","name":"Alcaraz - Mensik Laver Cup [1296x729]","credit":"Photo by ANDY RAIN/EPA/Shutterstock","height":729,"width":1296,"url":"https://a.espncdn.com/photo/2026/0925/r1721857_1296x729_16-9.jpg"}],"categories":[{"id":409224,"type":"topic","guid":"52313677-19f8-b106-ec91-d8d17e6087fe","description":"news","sportId":0,"topicId":781},{"id":9581,"type":"league","uid":"s:850","guid":"aa07e63d-cf6e-3705-9c8d-8d5208e6af14","description":"Tennis","sportId":850,"leagueId":850,"league":{"id":850,"description":"Tennis","links":{"mobile":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/"}},"web":{"leagues":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/"}}}}},{"id":463146,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:850~l:851~a:3782","guid":"07843754-8bdf-63b0-5983-24252738169e","description":"Carlos Alcaraz","sportId":851,"athleteId":3782,"athlete":{"id":3782,"description":"Carlos Alcaraz","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/player/_/id/3782/carlos-alcaraz"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/player/_/id/3782/carlos-alcaraz"}}}}},{"id":641317,"type":"athlete","uid":"s:850~l:851~a:10319","guid":"589e3a11-e409-3279-bf74-b8660578c1e7","description":"Jakub Mensik","sportId":851,"athleteId":10319,"athlete":{"id":10319,"description":"Jakub Mensik","links":{"mobile":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/player/_/id/10319/jakub-mensik"}},"web":{"athletes":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/player/_/id/10319/jakub-mensik"}}}}}],"keywords":["news","Tennis","Carlos Alcaraz","Jakub Mensik"],"story":"<p>LONDON -- <a data-player-guid=\"07843754-8bdf-63b0-5983-24252738169e\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=3782\">Carlos Alcaraz</a> and doubles partner <a data-player-guid=\"589e3a11-e409-3279-bf74-b8660578c1e7\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=10319\">Jakub Mensik</a> gave Team Europe a 3-1 lead over Team World after the opening day of the Laver Cup on Friday.</p>\n<p>Alcaraz and Mensik beat <a data-player-guid=\"60870ae1-bd80-2afa-54ea-e8b8a5d5fd7e\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2865\">Alexander Bublik</a> and <a data-player-guid=\"6493155f-cacc-7aa5-ba78-d952efa4c652\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2946\">Taylor Fritz</a> 6-4, 6-4 in the final match of the day at the O2 Arena.</p>\n<p><a data-player-guid=\"14a740e2-9290-3b00-84d2-8a65c9754208\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=12657\">Rafael Jodar</a> had broken a 1-1 deadlock after the day session by defeating Bublik 6-2, 6-3 in the evening's singles match.</p>\n<p>In the day session, <a data-player-guid=\"b55524e2-a931-d142-f794-50b742380e8e\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=3774\">Brandon Nakashima</a> made the most of his Laver Cup debut by beating Mensik 6-1, 3-6, 10-7.</p>\n<p>The 16th-ranked Nakashima was a late addition to Andre Agassi's roster after U.S. Open runner-up <a data-player-guid=\"2358bec1-f6f0-3540-a37e-13bc322d2c08\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=9250\">Ben Shelton</a> withdrew last week.</p>\n<p>In the event's opener, <a data-player-guid=\"116ef01e-3239-e44f-9c8a-022f81012782\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2989\">Casper Ruud</a> beat <a data-player-guid=\"d24f1930-30b5-f246-e9d4-4f40c6853a90\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=3700\">Francisco Cerundolo</a> 6-7 (4), 6-4, 10-8 to give Europe an early lead.</p>\n<p>There are four matches per day in the three-day event.</p>\n<p>Wins are worth one point on Friday, two points on Saturday and three points on Sunday. The first team to reach 13 points wins.</p>\n<p>Europe has won the Laver Cup five times while Team World took its third title in last year's edition of the Ryder Cup-style event.</p>\n\n\n\n\n","allowAMP":true,"allowAds":true,"allowComments":true,"allowCommerce":true,"allowContentReactions":true,"allowSearch":true,"isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/50029830"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=50029830"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/general/tennis/story?storyId=50029830"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/story/_/id/50029830/alcaraz-mensik-doubles-win-gives-team-europe-3-1-laver-cup-lead-team-world"}},"premium":false},{"id":49953284,"nowId":"1-49953284","contentKey":"49953284-1-5-1","dataSourceIdentifier":"6e537ca6d1d31","publishedkey":"49953284","type":"HeadlineNews","feedDisplayType":"Default","headline":"US Open men's final draws record audience of 3.2 million","description":"The US Open men's final between champion Alexander Zverev and American Ben Shelton averaged 3.2 million viewers on ABC, the largest viewership for that match since ESPN's family of networks began televising the tournament in 2009.","title":"US Open men's final draws record audience of 3.2 million","linkText":"US Open men's final watched by record 3.2M; Tiafoe-Shelton averaged 3.1M","categorized":"2026-09-16T01:39:54Z","originallyPosted":"2026-09-16T00:51:03Z","lastModified":"2026-09-16T01:39:52Z","published":"2026-09-16T01:39:52Z","root":"tennis","section":"Tennis","source":"Associated Press","images":[{