ATP","Ben Shelton","Alexander Zverev","Carlos Alcaraz","Elena Rybakina","Aryna Sabalenka"],"story":"<p>NEW YORK -- The <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/tennis/story/_/id/49933388/alexander-zverev-beats-ben-shelton-4-sets-win-2026-us-open\" target=\"_blank\">US Open men's final</a> between champion <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2375\">Alexander Zverev</a> and American <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=9250\">Ben Shelton</a> averaged 3.2 million viewers on ABC, the largest viewership for that match since ESPN's family of networks began televising the tournament in 2009.</p>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/tennis/story?id=49920080&_slug_=elena-rybakina-world-no-1-secures-first-us-open-title\" target=\"_blank\">women's final</a> -- won by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=3126\">Elena Rybakina</a> over <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=3038\">Aryna Sabalenka</a> -- averaged 2.7 million and was up 13% from last year, ESPN said Tuesday.</p>\n<p>The quarterfinals averaged 1.3 million viewers on ESPN. The <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/tennis/story?id=49877286&_slug_=ben-shelton-stuns-carlos-alcaraz-5-set-late-night-epic-make-us-open-semifinals\" target=\"_blank\">latest-finishing match in US Open history</a> between <a data-player-guid=\"07843754-8bdf-63b0-5983-24252738169e\" href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=3782\">Carlos Alcaraz</a> and Shelton averaged 1.6 million, with 967,000 viewers staying with the broadcast even during the match's final moments from 3:30 a.m. to 3:40 a.m. ET.</p>\n<p>The <a href=\"https://www.espn.com/tennis/story?id=49909945&_slug_=ben-shelton-beats-frances-tiafoe-all-american-semifinal-reach-2026-us-open-final\" target=\"_blank\">semifinal featuring Americans</a> <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/sports/tennis/players/profile?playerId=2708\">Frances Tiafoe</a> and Shelton averaged 3.1 million viewers and was the largest men's semifinal audience for ESPN.</p>\n<p>ESPN's full US Open coverage averaged 1.2 million viewers, the largest audience since 2022.</p>\n\n\n\n\n","allowAMP":true,"allowAds":true,"allowComments":true,"allowCommerce":true,"allowContentReactions":true,"allowSearch":true,"isLiveBlog":false,"links":{"api":{"self":{"href":"https://content.core.api.espn.com/v1/sports/news/49953284"}},"app":{"sportscenter":{"href":"sportscenter://x-callback-url/showStory?uid=49953284"}},"mobile":{"href":"http://m.espn.go.com/general/tennis/story?storyId=49953284"},"web":{"href":"https://www.espn.com/tennis/story/_/id/49953284/us-open-men-final-alexander-zverev-ben-shelton-draws-record-audience"}},"premium":false}],"breakingNews":[],"timestamp":"2026-09-30T12:24:55Z","status":"success"}